[Event "French: Advance"]

{The French (1...e6 2...d5) concedes space but builds a solid chain. Black's plan is always to attack the base of White's chain with ...c5 and ...f6.}
1. e4 {Centre. The pawn on e4 controls d5.}
1... e6 {[%csl Gd5] The French: prepares ...d5. The pawn on e6 controls d5.}
2. d4 {Builds a centre. The pawn on d4 controls e5.}
2... d5 {[%cal Gd5e4] Challenges e4. The pawn on d5 eyes the pawn on e4.}
3. e5 {The Advance: gains space.}
3... c5 {[%cal Gc5d4] Attacks the base of the chain. The pawn on c5 eyes the pawn on d4.}
4. c3 {Supports d4.}
4... Nc6 {More pressure on d4. The knight on c6 eyes the pawn on e5 and the pawn on d4.}
5. Nf3 {Supports d4.}
5... Qb6 {[%cal Gb6d4,Gb6b2] Piles up on d4 and eyes b2. The queen on b6 eyes the pawn on b2.}
6. a3 {Prepares b4.}
 (6. Bd3 {The Milner-Barry Gambit. The bishop on d3 eyes the pawn on h7 and controls e4.}
6... cxd4 {Takes. The pawn on d4 eyes the pawn on c3.}
7. cxd4 {Recaptures.}
7... Bd7 {Prepares ...Nxd4 and avoids Bb5+.}
8. O-O {Gambits the d4 pawn. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
8... Nxd4 {Accepts. The knight on d4 eyes the knight on f3.}
9. Nxd4 {Trades. The knight on d4 eyes the pawn on e6.}
9... Qxd4 {Takes. The queen on d4 eyes the pawn on e5 and the bishop on d3 and controls e4.}
10. Nc3 {Develops with compensation. The knight on c3 eyes the pawn on d5 and controls e4.}
)
6... c4 {[%csl Gc4] Locks the queenside to stop b4.}
7. Nbd2 {Develops. The knight on d2 eyes the pawn on c4 and controls e4.}
7... Na5 {[%cal Ga5b3] Eyes b3.} *

[Event "French: Winawer"]

{The Winawer (3...Bb4) pins the knight and often gives up the bishop pair to damage White's structure.}
1. e4 {Centre. The pawn on e4 controls d5.}
1... e6 {French. The pawn on e6 controls d5.}
2. d4 {Centre. The pawn on d4 controls e5.}
2... d5 {Challenges e4. The pawn on d5 eyes the pawn on e4.}
3. Nc3 {Defends e4. The knight on c3 eyes the pawn on d5.}
3... Bb4 {[%cal Gb4c3] The Winawer: pins the knight. The bishop on b4 eyes the knight on c3.}
4. e5 {Gains space.}
4... c5 {Hits d4. The pawn on c5 eyes the pawn on d4.}
5. a3 {Asks the bishop. The pawn on a3 eyes the bishop on b4.}
5... Bxc3+ {Gives up the bishop pair. The bishop on c3 eyes the pawn on d4 and the pawn on b2. It is check, so the reply is forced.}
6. bxc3 {Doubled pawns.}
6... Ne7 {Develops, ready to meet Qg4.}
7. Qg4 {[%cal Gg4g7] Hits g7. The queen on g4 eyes the pawn on g7 and the pawn on e6 and controls e4.}
 (7. Nf3 {The positional approach.}
7... Qa5 {[%cal Ga5c3] Pins the c3 pawn. The queen on a5 eyes the pawn on a3 and the pawn on c3.}
8. Bd2 {Unpins.}
8... Nbc6 {Develops. The knight on c6 eyes the pawn on e5 and the pawn on d4.}
9. Be2 {Develops.}
)
7... Qc7 {Counterattacks. The queen on c7 eyes the pawn on e5.}
8. Qxg7 {Takes. The queen on g7 eyes the rook on h8 and the pawn on f7.}
8... Rg8 {Hits the queen. The rook on g8 eyes the queen on g7.}
9. Qxh7 {Takes. The queen on h7 eyes the rook on g8 and the pawn on f7 and controls e4.}
9... cxd4 {Counterattack in the centre. The pawn on d4 eyes the pawn on c3.}
10. Ne2 {Develops. The knight on e2 eyes the pawn on d4.}
10... Nbc6 {Develops. The knight on c6 eyes the pawn on e5.}
11. f4 {Protects e5.} *

[Event "French: Tarrasch & Exchange"]

{Against 3.Nd2 Black plays ...c5. Against the Exchange, develop actively.}
1. e4 {Centre. The pawn on e4 controls d5.}
1... e6 {French. The pawn on e6 controls d5.}
2. d4 {Centre. The pawn on d4 controls e5.}
2... d5 {Challenges. The pawn on d5 eyes the pawn on e4.}
3. Nd2 {The Tarrasch.}
 (3. exd5 {The Exchange. The pawn on d5 eyes the pawn on e6.}
3... exd5 {Recaptures; the c8-bishop is free. The pawn on d5 controls e4.}
4. Nf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 controls e5.}
4... Nf6 {Develops. The knight on f6 controls e4.}
5. Bd3 {Develops. The bishop on d3 eyes the pawn on h7 and controls e4.}
5... Bd6 {Develops. The bishop on d6 eyes the pawn on h2 and controls e5.}
6. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
6... O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
)
3... c5 {[%cal Gc5d4] Hits d4. The pawn on c5 eyes the pawn on d4.}
4. exd5 {Takes. The pawn on d5 eyes the pawn on e6.}
4... Qxd5 {Recaptures. The queen on d5 eyes the pawn on d4 and the pawn on a2 and controls e4 and e5.}
5. Ngf3 {Develops. The knight on f3 controls e5.}
5... cxd4 {Takes.}
6. Bc4 {[%cal Gc4d5] Gains time on the queen. The bishop on c4 eyes the queen on d5.}
6... Qd6 {Retreats. The queen on d6 eyes the pawn on h2 and controls d5 and e5.}
7. O-O {Castles. The king is safe and the rook comes into play.}
7... Nf6 {Develops. The knight on f6 controls d5 and e4.}
8. Nb3 {Hunts d4. The knight on b3 eyes the pawn on d4.}
8... Nc6 {Defends. The knight on c6 controls e5.}
9. Nbxd4 {Recaptures. The knight on d4 eyes the knight on c6 and the pawn on e6.}
9... a6 {Stops Nb5.} *
